Send_Payments_Unit_Concrete_Test
├── when a call into Payments is already running
│   └── it should revert with ReentrantCall
└── when no call is running
    ├── when the recipient or the token is the zero address
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
    ├── when the recipient is Payments itself
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidRecipient
    ├── when the amount is 0
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroAmount
    ├── when the payment id is zero
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroPaymentId
    ├── when the document hash is zero
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroDocumentHash
    ├── when the job nonce is zero
    │   └── it should revert with ZeroJobNonce
    └── when every field is set
        ├── when the supplied payment id is not paymentId of the item
        │   └── it should revert with PaymentIdMismatch
        ├── when the item names an executor and the caller is someone else
        │   └── it should revert with InvalidExecutor
        ├── when this payment id was already paid
        │   └── it should revert with PaymentIdConsumed
        ├── when the token has no code
        │   └── it should revert with TokenHasNoCode
        └── when the payment is new and the token is a contract
            ├── when the token's transferFrom reverts
            │   └── it should bubble up the token's revert data unchanged
            ├── when the token's transferFrom returns false
            │   └── it should revert with TokenCallReturnedFalse
            ├── when the token's transferFrom returns nothing
            │   └── it should accept it and still check the exact balance
            ├── when the token re-enters send or sendBatch during transferFrom
            │   └── it should revert the inner call with ReentrantCall
            ├── when the recipient receives a different amount
            │   └── it should revert with InexactTransfer
            ├── given the recipient is the caller
            │   └── it should require the balance not to change
            ├── given the payment reverts for any reason
            │   └── it should leave the payment id unpaid
            └── when the recipient receives exactly the amount
                ├── it should mark the payment id as paid
                ├── it should leave Payments' own balance unchanged
                └── it should emit PaymentSent
